{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/categoryhero_pairpreview

    The preview of the colour pair, the last row of the colours section of the
    category appearance form: the category's own name set on the solid band, in
    the colours that are stored.

    It is TEXT on a coloured box and not a picture, so it carries no image role
    and nothing is hidden from a screen reader: the caption under the name is
    ordinary visible text saying what the box is.

    The form renders this with the stored pair, so it is correct with JavaScript
    switched off and never disagrees with the two fields above it. With the
    module running, the categoryhero AMD module writes the two colours into this
    element's style as they are typed, from the same valid-hex path that drives
    the swatch - an invalid value leaves the last valid pair on the band.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * name - the category's name, in the PLAIN spelling (this template escapes it)
    * style - the band's declarations, built by the form from branding::hex() alone

    The style value is the one CSS-context sink of this template: Mustache escaping
    does not protect that context, so the form is what constrains the value to a
    pair of hex colours, and nothing here may put anything else into that attribute.

    Data-region hook the module addresses:
    * dim-pair-preview - the band itself, whose two colours the module writes

    @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Example context (json):
    {
        "name": "Departamento de Brigada Regional",
        "style": "background-color: #0a4a85; color: #ffffff;"
    }
}}
<div class="dim-pair-preview" data-region="dim-pair-preview" style="{{style}}">
    <span class="dim-pair-preview__name">{{name}}</span>
    <small class="dim-pair-preview__caption">
        {{#str}}categoryhero_pairpreview, theme_dimensions{{/str}}
    </small>
</div>
